      "beat_id": "B04",
      "act": "MECHANISM",
      "role_note": "The four behaviours batch.py guarantees, one card each.",
      "narration_text": "Four rules shape a batch. First, every entry is checked before anything runs, and all the problems are reported together. Second, each app gets its own folder, so one crash is recorded, and the rest carry on. Third, apps can run in parallel, but the U.I. checks share one container, so they take turns. Fourth, one summary at the end.",
      "voice": "am_onyx",
      "engine": "kokoro",
      "estimated_duration_s": 23.1,
